  "adaptations": [
    "Reuse compiled Style and the existing hex/color/option parser; public Color retains compiled sequences after process mode changes.",
    "Reuse existing rustix 1.1.6 with termios/stdio features: native stdin device queries instead of repeated stty subprocess parsing; stdio enables the real recovery consumer without unsafe descriptor manipulation. Only successful dimensions are cached.",
    "The terminal color mode is process-wide and may be forced/reset; no per-request or per-application mode pretending. COLUMNS/LINES override dimensions on each call.",
    "Public flat console exports follow existing native SDK layout. Explicit new arguments and Default replace optional constructor arguments.",
    "Windows ANSICON/native console and real Windows tty execution remain in release acceptance; no Windows execution claimed by Darwin/PTY results."
  ],
